guidebook-SOP-desc = [bold]Standard Operating Procedures[/bold] (abbr. [italic]SOP[/italic]) are a set of guidelines that must be followed in the corresponding circumstances. Violating SOP may be grounds for demotion or dismissal.

guidebook-SOP-infobox-main =
    Standard operating procedures are not the same as [textlink="server rules" link="CorvaxRuleset"], and punishments for violating them should be handled in-character.
    OOC punishment from administration may follow in cases of systematic or serious SOP violations without a clear reason.

    Stricter requirements apply to security officers, command members, legal department staff, CentComm, and DSO. These roles are tightly tied to SOP and Corporate Law, so even a minor SOP violation without logical justification may lead to a rules-related punishment.
    This does not mean that all violations by the roles above must be ignored by other characters. Violations should be handled appropriately in-character.

    General SOP must be followed to the same extent as departmental SOP.

